BT 1 0 0 1 0 71 Tm /F6+0 11.5 Tf 16.5 TL (In the shoe-salesman story, nobody wears shoes. Is that \004no chance\005 or a \004splendid opportunity\005? The) Tj T* (same situation draws opposite responses. Drawing on Carol Dweck, the lectures set a fixed mindset) Tj T* (against a growth mindset. People with a fixed mindset avoid challenges, resist change, dwell on their) Tj T* -0.004567 Tw (limits, reject criticism and stop learning once school is over. Growth-mindset people welcome challenges,) Tj T* 0 Tw (learn from failure and treat learning as lifelong.) Tj T* ET
