BT 1 0 0 1 0 104 Tm /F6+0 11.5 Tf 16.5 TL (Time can\001t really be managed. What we manage is our habits and our perception of it. Monochronic) Tj T* (people stick to rigid schedules, while polychronic people stay flexible. Others tend to judge our) Tj T* (personality by our punctuality and by how we behave under deadline pressure. To control time, log it,) Tj T* -0.003544 Tw (look for \004time leakage\005 \(interruptions, indecision, poor organisation, social media, unmanaged email\) and) Tj T* 0 Tw (make room for productive work. Working at your biological peak time helps. Covey\001s urgent/important) Tj T* (quadrants and the 80/20 Pareto principle help with prioritising, and \004time stealers\005 such as waiting and) Tj T* (travel can be turned into \004time gifters.\005) Tj T* ET
