BT 1 0 0 1 0 30.4 Tm /F5+0 9.8 Tf 13.4 TL (Pongal is the most important harvest festival of Tamil Nadu. It is celebrated in mid-January to thank the Sun) Tj T* (God, the rain and the cattle for a good harvest. The festival lasts four days: Bhogi, Thai Pongal, Mattu Pongal) Tj T* (and Kaanum Pongal.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 54 418.5898 cm
q
.066667 .094118 .152941 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 57.2 Tm /F5+0 9.8 Tf 13.4 TL (On Bhogi, families clean their homes and throw away old things. On Thai Pongal, they draw colourful kolams at) Tj T* (the entrance and cook fresh rice and milk in a new clay pot in the open yard. When the milk boils over, everyone) Tj T* (shouts "Pongalo Pongal!" The pot is decorated with turmeric plants and sugarcane. The festive meal includes) Tj T* -0.110358 Tw (sakkarai pongal, venn pongal, sambar, vadai and payasam, served on banana leaves. On Mattu Pongal, farmers) Tj T* 0 Tw (decorate and worship their cattle, and Kaanum Pongal is a day for family visits and community games.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 54 347.0898 cm
q
.066667 .094118 .152941 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 57.2 Tm /F5+0 9.8 Tf 13.4 TL (Modern eco-friendly practices can preserve the core spirit of the festival. Instead of burning plastic and old tyres) Tj T* (on Bhogi, communities can burn only dry leaves or turn them into compost, which reduces smoke and air) Tj T* (pollution. Clay pots, banana leaves and areca-leaf plates can replace plastic and thermocol, and kolams can be) Tj T* (drawn with natural rice flour. Villages can organise tree-planting drives, rainwater harvesting and cloth-bag) Tj T* (campaigns during the festival, and use solar lamps instead of excess electric decorations.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 54 315.7898 cm
q
.066667 .094118 .152941 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 17 Tm /F5+0 9.8 Tf 13.4 TL (In this way, Pongal can remain joyful and traditional while staying kind to nature, and the next generation will) Tj T* (learn that celebration and conservation can go together.) Tj T* ET
