q
.066667 .094118 .152941 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 70.6 Tm /F5+0 9.8 Tf 13.4 TL (The festival begins with flag hoisting and several days of processions. On the car day, devotees of all ages hold) Tj T* (thick ropes and pull the heavy chariot together through the four main streets, chanting prayers while drums and) Tj T* (nadaswaram fill the air. This shared effort is a strong symbol of unity, because people from every community) Tj T* (take part. Women draw kolams on the road, and families offer coconuts, bananas and flowers to the deity.) Tj T* (Volunteers give free food such as pongal, puliyodharai, curd rice and sweet payasam as prasadam, served on) Tj T* (leaves.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 54 58.7898 cm
q
.066667 .094118 .152941 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 70.6 Tm /F5+0 9.8 Tf 13.4 TL (However, such a large crowd also creates problems. Single-use plastic cups, plates and bags litter the streets,) Tj T* (and loudspeakers cause noise pollution. Eco-friendly measures can solve these problems. Organisers can ban) Tj T* (single-use plastic and provide steel tumblers, banana leaves and paper bags. Dustbins and waste-sorting points) Tj T* (can be placed along the route, and volunteers can collect and compost the food waste. Noise can be controlled) Tj T* (by limiting loudspeaker volume and using traditional instruments. Barricades, marked entry and exit lanes,) Tj T* (volunteers, and first-aid points can manage the crowd safely.) Tj T* ET
