.066667 .094118 .152941 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 57.2 Tm /F5+0 9.8 Tf 13.4 TL (On arrival, a site engineer will give a short briefing on how the hybrid plant works. The wind turbines turn on tall) Tj T* (towers, and their blades rotate a generator inside the nacelle. We will watch how the strong coastal wind drives) Tj T* (them, and how the blades adjust their angle with the wind speed. In the solar section, we will observe rows of) Tj T* (photovoltaic panels, inverters and transformers that feed power into the grid. The control room will show how the) Tj T* (two sources balance each other: solar power peaks in the afternoon, whereas wind is strong in the evening and) Tj T* ET
