BT 1 0 0 1 0 3.6 Tm /F3+0 9.8 Tf 13.4 TL (Cloud Computing versus On-Premise Physical Data Centers for Engineering Enterprises) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 54 240.4898 cm
q
.066667 .094118 .152941 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 17 Tm /F5+0 9.8 Tf 13.4 TL (Engineering enterprises must decide whether to run their systems on the cloud or in their own physical data) Tj T* (centers. Both choices have strengths and weaknesses.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 54 195.7898 cm
q
.066667 .094118 .152941 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 30.4 Tm /F5+0 9.8 Tf 13.4 TL (Upfront capital expenditure is the clearest difference. Cloud services need almost no initial investment, because) Tj T* (companies simply pay for what they use. On-premise data centers, in contrast, require heavy spending on) Tj T* (servers, cooling systems, power backup and buildings before any work begins.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 54 151.0898 cm
q
.066667 .094118 .152941 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 30.4 Tm /F5+0 9.8 Tf 13.4 TL (As for recurring overheads, cloud bills can grow quickly if usage is not monitored, whereas an on-premise setup) Tj T* (has predictable costs once it is built, although it still needs staff, electricity and maintenance. Therefore, cloud) Tj T* (suits changing workloads, while on-premise suits stable and long-term demand.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 54 106.3898 cm
q
.066667 .094118 .152941 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 30.4 Tm /F5+0 9.8 Tf 13.4 TL (Workload scalability strongly favours the cloud. Companies can add computing power in minutes during) Tj T* (simulations or product launches and reduce it afterwards. On the other hand, on-premise systems have fixed) Tj T* (capacity, so expanding them takes weeks or months and leaves hardware idle during quiet periods.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 54 61.6898 cm
q
.066667 .094118 .152941 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 30.4 Tm /F5+0 9.8 Tf 13.4 TL (Data security and compliance are more complex. On-premise data centers give the company full physical) Tj T* (control, which is important for defence, healthcare or confidential design data. Cloud providers offer strong) Tj T* (security tools and certifications, but the company depends on a third party and must follow data-location laws) Tj T* ET
